    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1204581\">Jace</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Formalisation.20of.20a.20trivial.20inequality/near/625694677\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also how would you write that if for all finite p and q that p/q =/= A that A is irrational?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You can take a look at how mathlib says it <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=irrational_iff_ne_rational#doc\">docs#irrational_iff_ne_rational</a> (as well as the definition of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Irrational#doc\">docs#Irrational</a> itself)</p>",
        "id": 625696848,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1789986256
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"366779\">Jz Pan</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Formalisation.20of.20a.20trivial.20inequality/near/625660232\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873350\">Weiyi Wang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Formalisation.20of.20a.20trivial.20inequality/near/625625003\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span aria-label=\"stuck out tongue wink\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f61c\" role=\"img\" title=\"stuck out tongue wink\">:stuck_out_tongue_wink:</span> What if <code>(p q : ℤ)</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Then what is <code>p / q</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It is Euclidean division <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Int.ediv#doc\">docs#Int.ediv</a>, which incidently also makes the statement true, but it needs a different lemma to prove</p>",
